    "result_text": "No `membershipTier` references remain. The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string membership **tier** with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133).\n\n**Level formula:** start at 1; +1 when an email is present; +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`; capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure). The example test owner (email present, unique name \u2192 namesakeCount 0) yields `1 + 1 + 1 = 3`. \u2713\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` (string) schema property with `membershipLevel` (integer, min 1 / max 3), so the generated `OwnerDto` now exposes `membershipLevel` instead of `membershipTier`.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 swapped the `@Mapping` target to `membershipLevel` and replaced `membershipTier(Owner)` with `membershipLevel(Owner)` implementing the new numeric rule. The old logic keyed off `householdSize` for a GOLD tier; the new level uses only `email` and `namesakeCount` per the spec.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` (using the mapper) instead of/in addition to the prior fields, per \"anything that recorded the tier \u2026 must record the level instead\"; updated the audit logger doc comment and removed the now-stale \"drives the GOLD membership tier\" comment.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The audit log confirms `membershipLevel=3` at creation.\n\nOne note: the `householdSize` field is still computed and stored on the owner but no longer feeds any tier/level (it previously drove GOLD). I left the field in place since removing persisted state was outside the scope of this change; let me know if you'd like it cleaned up.",
